    "text": "Which of the following transformations is seen in spermiogenesis?",
    "explanation": "Spermiogenesis or spermateleosis is the process of maturation of spermatids to spermatozoa. It is the final stage of spermatogenesis. \r\nThe major events occurring during spermiogenesis include: \r\n• Nuclear morphogenesis and condensation \r\n• Formation of tail \r\n• Formation of acrosome \r\n• Rearrangement of organelles (mitochondria, centrioles, etc.) \r\n• Shedding off excess cytoplasm",
