    "id": "ANAT-003-000001-I",
    "subject": "Anatomy",
    "text": "Formation of which of the following indicates the beginning of gastrulation?",
    "explanation": "The formation of the primitive streak from the epiblast is an indicator of the beginning of gastrulation. \r\nBy the 15th day of development, some epiblast cells lying along the central axis, near the tail end of the embryonic disc, begin to proliferate. These proliferated cells form an elevation called primitive streak that bulges into the amniotic cavity. \r\nGastrulation is the process that forms all the 3 germ layers namely, ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm in the embryo. It occurs during the 3rd week of gestation. The image given below shows the formation of primitive streak.",
