    "subject": "Anatomy",
    "text": "Which of the following statements regarding intraembryonic mesoderm is false?",
    "explanation": "The intraembryonic mesoderm spreads throughout the embryonic disc, except in the region of the prechordal plate and cloacal membrane. In these two regions, the ectoderm is in direct contact with the endoderm. \r\nThe image given below shows the direct contact of intraembryonic mesoderm with the endoderm. \r\nThe intraembryonic mesoderm or secondary mesoderm is formed by the invagination and movement of epiblast cells between the newly formed endoderm and the epiblast. In the later stages of development, the ectoderm and endoderm mostly persist as lining epithelium. Mesoderm forms most of the tissues of the body, including bone, cartilage, connective tissue, muscles (skeletal, smooth, cardiac), blood, lymph, and cardiovascular organs.",
